`strings` of the ELF: **0** `__sec_sink__`. WT source has **1**.

### `c_secret_scan_call` — 4 compares, first-RPAREN return
Immediates (only): `LPAREN` @ `0x45e050`, `RPAREN` @ `0x45e12e`,
`COMMA` @ `0x45e190`, `IDENT` @ `0x45e1d8`. **No** loop `LPAREN`.

```
0x45e14a  oo_str_eq  RPAREN
0x45e151  je   0x45e190     ; not equal → try COMMA
          … restore regs …
0x45e187  jmp  oo_str_release ; EQUAL → return (scan over)
0x45e1b3  add  $1, %r14      ; COMMA → argi++  (no depth==1 test)
```

WT would compare `LPAREN` again inside the loop and only stop `RPAREN`
when `depth <= 0`. This body cannot do that.

### `check_secret_println_sinks` println walker — LPAREN×1, RPAREN exits
Token-kind counts inside the function: `LPAREN` **1**, `RPAREN` **1**,
`IDENT` **3**, `COMMA` **0**, `println` **1**, `eprintln` **1**.

Walker after `c_secret_resolve_alias` + sid `println`/`eprintln`:

```
0x476608  lit LPAREN
0x47660d  add  $2, %rbx          ; p = i+1, then maybe skip
0x47665f  oo_str_eq LPAREN
0x476666  cmove %rbp, %rbx       ; if NOT LPAREN, do not skip
0x47666a  loop head
0x476675  lit RPAREN
0x4766c8  oo_str_eq RPAREN
0x4766cf  jne  0x475f30          ; EQUAL → leave walker (next sink ifs)
0x4766d5  lit IDENT
0x47672c  oo_str_eq IDENT
0x476733  jne  0x476db0          ; EQUAL → resolve + refuse
0x476739  mov  %rbp, %rbx        ; else p+1
0x47673c  jmp  0x47666a          ; back to RPAREN — never LPAREN
```

`0x475f30` is the `write_file` / `fetch` / … sequential `if sid ==`
cascade (HEAD dispatch, not the WT `else if` / `__sec_sink__` chain).

A depth walker would increment a local on loop-`LPAREN` and only take
the `0x475f30` exit when depth hits 0. There is **no** such local.

### `c_emit_println` — still flat (source **and** host)
Stmt belt was **not** part of the wave-2 hunk (`c_emit_print.oo`
HEAD-clean). ELF string compares: `LPAREN`×1, `RPAREN`×3, `COMMA`×2,
`SEMI`×2, `IDENT`×1, `__sec__`×1. Matches L14–28: per-arg walk
`break`s on first `COMMA`/`RPAREN`/`SEMI`, then `c_emit_expr_c`
(depth-correct emit) for that truncated span.

Consequence:

- `println((1), tok)` — first arg is `(1)` (no SECRET IDENT); after
  `c_emit_expr_c` the COMMA is seen; second arg `tok` refused. emit-c
  **BLOCK** without depth. Front-door still **FN**.
- `println(("x") + tok)` — IDENT scan stops at the grouping `RPAREN`;
  never sees `tok`; `c_emit_expr_c` then lowers the **whole** concat
  (it is depth-aware). emit-c **leaks**. Front-door **FN**. WT depth
  on the front-door would refuse this on check / emit-c / llvm
  **before** the stmt belt. Host cannot.


